A learner encounters this problem. What value does this procedure return?
int[] a = {2, 4, 2, -4, 0, 5, 3};
int acc = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) if (a[i] > 5) acc++;
return acc;

Review the case and choose wisely. What does this string routine return?
String s = "cdaubexe";
int acc = 0, target = 'x';
for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) if (s.charAt(i) == target) acc++;
return acc;

Think through this worked case. Which index pair does this scan return?
int[] a = {1, 2, 3, 4, 7, 11, 14, 18, 21};
int i = 0, j = a.length - 1;
while (i < j) { int s = a[i] + a[j]; if (s == 5) return new int[]{i, j}; if (s < 5) i++; else j--; }
return new int[]{-1, -1};

Across a field survey, a registrar notes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. Evaluate the example that follows. What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(35);
Node b = new Node(10);
Node c = new Node(15);
a.next = b; b.next = c; c.next = null;
Node p = a;
while (p.next != null) p = p.next;
return p.value;

In a training module, a registrar notes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. Tracing this code:
int[] a = {5, 6, 10, 15, 18, 23, 28, 30, 34, 37};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 38) return steps; if (a[mid] < 38) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return steps; Which answer is correct for this case?

During a quality review, a registrar notes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. What value does this procedure return?
int[] a = {7, -4, 5, 8, 2, 5, 8, 0};
int acc = 1;
for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) if (a[i] != 0) acc *= a[i];
return acc;

In a service manual, a registrar notes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. Evaluate the following carefully. What does this string routine return?
String s = "cbozzobc";
int i = 0, j = s.length() - 1;
while (i < j) { if (s.charAt(i) != s.charAt(j)) return false; i++; j--; }
return true;

Reason step by step to answer. Which index pair does this scan return?
int[] a = {-2, 2, 6, 9, 11, 14, 15, 19};
int i = 0, j = a.length - 1;
while (i < j) { int s = a[i] + a[j]; if (s == 29) return new int[]{i, j}; if (s < 29) i++; else j--; }
return new int[]{-1, -1};

